## Color rules

### Use semantic tokens, never raw hex in UI components

**Wrong:**
```tsx
// ❌ hardcoded hex in component styling
<div className="bg-[#f5f6f8] dark:bg-[#1a1f2e] text-[#212121]" />
<div style={{ background: "#4f46e5", color: "#fff" }} />
```

**Right:**
```tsx
// ✓ semantic tokens from theme.css
<div className="bg-card text-foreground border-border" />
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground" />
<div className="bg-muted text-muted-foreground" />
```

### Dark mode — never hardcode dark variants

```tsx
// ❌
<div className="dark:bg-[#1e2533]" />

// ✓ — the token already handles dark mode
<div className="bg-background" />
```

### Exception: data-driven colors (inline styles only)

Hardcoded hex is **only acceptable** in `style={{ ... }}` when the color comes from user/config data and cannot be known at design time — for example, chart series colors from an API, or provider/tag colors stored in a database.

```tsx
// ✓ — runtime data color, no Tailwind alternative
<div style={{ borderLeftColor: provider.color, borderLeftWidth: 3 }} />
```

Do not use data-driven hex in `className` (Tailwind can't JIT-compile dynamic hex strings).

### Token palette (quick reference)

| Use case | Token |
|----------|-------|
| Page / canvas background | `bg-background` |
| Card surface | `bg-card` / `text-card-foreground` |
| Muted surface (L2 nav) | `bg-app-shell-l2-surface` |
| Sidebar | `bg-sidebar` |
| Primary action | `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground` |
| Muted text | `text-muted-foreground` |
| Borders | `border-border` / `border-app-shell-border` |
| Hover rows | `hover:bg-app-shell-l2-row-hover` |
| Selected rows | `bg-app-shell-l2-row-active` |
| Destructive | `bg-destructive` / `text-destructive` |

