## Modal + floating surfaces

- **No perimeter border** on `Dialog`, `Sheet`, `AlertDialog`, `Drawer` content, or `FLOATING_PANEL_SURFACE_CLASSNAME` (Popover, DropdownMenu, Select, profile popover) — use shadow for depth.
- Modal scrims: use `MODAL_OVERLAY_VISUAL_CLASS` from `modalOverlayClasses.ts`.
- Floating panels: use `FLOATING_PANEL_SURFACE_CLASSNAME` from `floatingPanelSurface.ts`.

---

## L2 navigation panels

All L2 panels must use `L2NavLayout` from [`L2NavLayout.v1.tsx`](src/app/components/L2NavLayout.v1.tsx). Do not build custom L2 scroll panels unless the product explicitly requires it (and even then, mirror the token classes exported from L2NavLayout).

- `PANEL` — standard L2 column with `border-r`
- `CHILD_ACTIVE` / `CHILD_INACTIVE` — section child rows
- `CHILD_FLAT_ACCENT_ACTIVE` — accent flat-nav rows (e.g. Agents → Outcomes)
- `SECTION_HEADER` — collapsible section headers
- `FOOTER_ROW_CLS` — header-action row (e.g. "New message")
- Section `children` accept `string | { label: string; key?: string; external?: boolean }` — pass `external: true` to render a trailing `ExternalLink` icon (visual only unless `onClick` is also wired).

---

## Icon stroke

All Lucide icons: `strokeWidth={1.6}` + `absoluteStrokeWidth` when the icon is not rendered at exactly 24 × 24 px. See [`.cursor/rules/icon-stroke-lucide.mdc`](./icon-stroke-lucide.mdc).

---

## Storybook-first

Every new component under `src/app/components/` **must** ship with a story in `src/stories/` in the same PR/response. Modified components must update their story. Do not consider a component task complete without a story. See [`.cursor/rules/storybook-story-required.mdc`](./storybook-story-required.mdc).

---

## Out of scope by default

- Hero-led marketing sites, campaign landings, blog/portfolio templates.
- Ad hoc hex palettes for static UI styling (use `theme.css` tokens).
- Inline `dark:` class variants using raw hex — always use token classes instead.

